Landed the architect's preferred correction (i) — the `js.rt/*` rename at all three sites — as commit `1697b257` on `exception-js-r1r3` (not merged, not pushed).

**Resolution rule established:** lookup is exact-symbol in `resolve-var` ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jsr13/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:116)): env → active (module) store → primitives → registry, with the registry leg building the dotted symbol, so `js.rt/retained-condition` from outside descends into the `js` entry and reads `[:bindings 'rt …]` = nil, then fails loudly. The brief's premise was wrong: the callers at `31287b17` read `js/*`, not `js.rt/*`, so the orchestrator's install-only rename was a guaranteed mismatch in both paths.

**Why not literal shape A:** deleting the stubs gave the arbiter 15F/9E — `undeclared-free {:name raise-protocol}` — because the linker's step-5a join ([linker.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jsr13/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:1086)) discharges lambda-body reads only against unconditional top-level definitions, and the conditional in-body `yin/def`s in `js/init!` discharge nothing. The rename keeps the stubs (re-keyed), so discharge, exports-absence, and post-init resolution all hold; the full evidence is in the findings.

